# Stripe Integration Playbook for brocco.ai (May 2026)

**Tiers:** Free (no card) → Solo $49/mo → Team $199/mo → Enterprise (sales)

---

## 1. Checkout Flow — Recommended: **Stripe-Hosted Checkout** (`mode=subscription`)

| Option | When to use | brocco.ai fit |
|---|---|---|
| **Hosted Checkout** | Default for SaaS. Stripe owns PCI, 3DS, Apple Pay, tax, fraud, localization. Redirect-based. | **PICK THIS** |
| **Embedded Checkout** | Brand-pixel-perfect signup; iframe on your domain. Same backend as hosted. | Second choice if marketing demands no redirect |
| **Custom Elements** | Only if you need to embed payment fields inside a multi-step wizard you fully control | Overkill — adds 2 weeks of work |
| **Payment Links** | Sales hands-off, one-time link in an email. No code. | Use ONLY for the "Talk to Sales" Enterprise tier (link generated by your CSM) |

**Why hosted for brocco.ai:** desktop+web app already redirects users for OAuth-style flows; the redirect to checkout.stripe.com is identical UX to that. Stripe ships features (Link, BNPL, Apple Pay) automatically — you do nothing. Stripe Checkout converts ~15-30% better than custom forms when measured (`stripe.com/payments/checkout`). One file of code vs Elements' ~300 LOC.

---

## 2. Vercel Edge — Products, Prices, Sessions, Portal

### File: `lib/stripe.ts`
```ts
import Stripe from 'stripe';

export const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_API_KEY!, {
  apiVersion: '2025-11-15.basil',
  typescript: true,
  // Edge-safe fetch client
  httpClient: Stripe.createFetchHttpClient(),
});

export const PRICES = {
  solo_monthly:  process.env.STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_MONTHLY!,
  solo_annual:   process.env.STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_ANNUAL!,
  team_monthly:  process.env.STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM_MONTHLY!,
  team_annual:   process.env.STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM_ANNUAL!,
};
```

### One-time bootstrap script: `scripts/seed-stripe.ts` (run with `bun` or `tsx` once)
```ts
import { stripe } from '../lib/stripe';

async function seed() {
  const solo = await stripe.products.create({
    name: 'brocco.ai Solo',
    description: 'Solo agentic AI desktop+web',
  });
  const team = await stripe.products.create({
    name: 'brocco.ai Team',
    description: 'Team collaboration + shared agents',
  });

  const prices = await Promise.all([
    stripe.prices.create({ product: solo.id, unit_amount: 4900,  currency: 'usd', recurring: { interval: 'month' }, lookup_key: 'solo_monthly' }),
    stripe.prices.create({ product: solo.id, unit_amount: 49000, currency: 'usd', recurring: { interval: 'year'  }, lookup_key: 'solo_annual'  }), // ~17% off
    stripe.prices.create({ product: team.id, unit_amount: 19900, currency: 'usd', recurring: { interval: 'month' }, lookup_key: 'team_monthly' }),
    stripe.prices.create({ product: team.id, unit_amount: 199000,currency: 'usd', recurring: { interval: 'year'  }, lookup_key: 'team_annual'  }),
  ]);
  console.log(prices.map(p => `${p.lookup_key}=${p.id}`).join('\n'));
}
seed();
```

### Edge route: `app/api/checkout/route.ts`
```ts
export const runtime = 'edge';
import { stripe, PRICES } from '@/lib/stripe';
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { tier, interval, userId, email } = await req.json() as {
    tier: 'solo'|'team'; interval: 'monthly'|'annual'; userId: string; email: string;
  };
  const priceId = PRICES[`${tier}_${interval}` as keyof typeof PRICES];

  // Reuse Stripe customer if you've stashed one in your DB; otherwise let Checkout create it
  const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
    mode: 'subscription',
    customer_email: email,
    client_reference_id: userId,             // critical: ties Stripe customer to your user row
    line_items: [{ price: priceId, quantity: 1 }],
    allow_promotion_codes: true,
    billing_address_collection: 'auto',
    automatic_tax: { enabled: true },        // turns on Stripe Tax — flip if you've enabled it
    subscription_data: {
      billing_mode: { type: 'flexible' },    // 2026 default; future-proofs proration behavior
      metadata: { userId, tier, interval },
    },
    success_url: `${process.env.APP_URL}/billing/success?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}`,
    cancel_url:  `${process.env.APP_URL}/pricing`,
  });
  return NextResponse.json({ url: session.url });
}
```

### Edge route: `app/api/portal/route.ts` (cancel / switch plan / update card — one-click)
```ts
export const runtime = 'edge';
import { stripe } from '@/lib/stripe';
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { getStripeCustomerId } from '@/lib/db';   // your DB lookup

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { userId } = await req.json();
  const customer = await getStripeCustomerId(userId); // string, e.g. "cus_..."

  const portal = await stripe.billingPortal.sessions.create({
    customer,
    return_url: `${process.env.APP_URL}/account`,
  });
  return NextResponse.json({ url: portal.url });
}
```

**Plan switching with proration** is fully handled by the Customer Portal (configure once in dashboard → Billing → Customer portal → enable "switch plans" + select your products). For programmatic switches:

```ts
const sub = await stripe.subscriptions.retrieve(subId);
await stripe.subscriptions.update(subId, {
  items: [{ id: sub.items.data[0].id, price: newPriceId }],
  proration_behavior: 'create_prorations',  // or 'always_invoice' to charge immediately
});
```

**Cancel** (let user keep access until period end — the canonical pattern):
```ts
await stripe.subscriptions.update(subId, { cancel_at_period_end: true });
```

---

## 3. Webhooks — Edge Runtime, Signature-Verified

**Minimum events:** `checkout.session.completed`, `customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`, `customer.subscription.deleted`, `invoice.paid`, `invoice.payment_failed`.

### `app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts`
```ts
export const runtime = 'edge';
import { stripe } from '@/lib/stripe';
import { upsertSubscription, markPastDue, revokeAccess } from '@/lib/db';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const sig = req.headers.get('stripe-signature')!;
  const body = await req.text();                            // raw body — do NOT json()

  let event;
  try {
    // Edge-compatible async verifier — required (the sync one uses Node crypto)
    event = await stripe.webhooks.constructEventAsync(
      body, sig, process.env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET!
    );
  } catch (err: any) {
    return new Response(`Webhook Error: ${err.message}`, { status: 400 });
  }

  switch (event.type) {
    case 'checkout.session.completed': {
      const s = event.data.object;
      await upsertSubscription({
        userId: s.client_reference_id!,
        stripeCustomerId: s.customer as string,
        stripeSubscriptionId: s.subscription as string,
        status: 'active',
      });
      break;
    }
    case 'customer.subscription.created':
    case 'customer.subscription.updated': {
      const sub = event.data.object;
      await upsertSubscription({
        stripeSubscriptionId: sub.id,
        stripeCustomerId: sub.customer as string,
        priceId: sub.items.data[0].price.id,
        status: sub.status,                                  // active|trialing|past_due|canceled|unpaid
        currentPeriodEnd: new Date(sub.current_period_end * 1000),
        cancelAtPeriodEnd: sub.cancel_at_period_end,
      });
      break;
    }
    case 'customer.subscription.deleted':
      await revokeAccess((event.data.object as any).id);
      break;
    case 'invoice.payment_failed':
      await markPastDue((event.data.object as any).subscription as string);
      break;
  }

  return new Response('ok', { status: 200 });
}
```

**Critical:** `constructEventAsync` (not `constructEvent`) — the sync version uses Node's `crypto` and breaks on Edge. Use `request.text()` not `.json()` or signature fails.

---

## 4. Free Tier Without Credit Card

**The 2026 pattern (Cursor / Linear / Lovable / Vercel v0):**

- **Hobby plan = no Stripe at all.** No customer object, no subscription. Just a row in your DB: `users.plan = 'free'` + a usage counter.
- **Track usage in Vercel KV (or Upstash Redis):** atomic INCR on every action that costs money (LLM call, agent run, deploy).
- **Reset monthly** with a key like `usage:{userId}:{YYYY-MM}` and a 32-day TTL — auto-expires, no cron.
- **Hard cap with soft warnings** at 80% / 100%.

```ts
// lib/usage.ts  (Edge-compatible)
import { kv } from '@vercel/kv';

const FREE_LIMITS = { agentRuns: 50, completions: 2000 };  // Cursor-style

export async function checkAndIncrement(userId: string, metric: keyof typeof FREE_LIMITS) {
  const key = `usage:${userId}:${metric}:${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,7)}`;
  const count = await kv.incr(key);
  if (count === 1) await kv.expire(key, 60 * 60 * 24 * 32);

  const limit = FREE_LIMITS[metric];
  if (count > limit) {
    return { allowed: false, count, limit, upgrade: true };
  }
  if (count >= limit * 0.8) {
    return { allowed: true, count, limit, warn: true };     // banner: "80% used → Upgrade"
  }
  return { allowed: true, count, limit };
}
```

**Push toward paid:** when `allowed=false`, return a 402 with `{ checkoutUrl }` from `/api/checkout` pre-built for the Solo tier. Linear locks features at limit; Cursor degrades to slow-only models; Lovable shows a hard paywall modal with the Stripe Checkout URL inline. **For brocco.ai: do what Linear does — block the action, show a modal that hits `/api/checkout?tier=solo&interval=monthly` directly.**

---

## 5. Annual Billing Toggle

**Pattern: one Price per `(tier × interval)`** — 4 prices total for brocco.ai. This is what every modern SaaS does (Linear, Vercel, Posthog all use distinct annual prices).

- **Why not Stripe's "flexible billing" alone?** Flexible billing is about proration math, not UI toggles. You still need separate Price IDs because annual prices are typically discounted (~17%) vs monthly × 12.
- **UI pattern:** a single toggle in the pricing component flips a `interval` state; the "Subscribe" button posts `{tier, interval}` to `/api/checkout`. The Checkout Session resolves the right Price ID server-side from the lookup table.
- **Sync UI ↔ Stripe:** use `lookup_keys` (`solo_monthly`, `solo_annual`, etc.) so you can fetch all prices via `stripe.prices.list({ lookup_keys: [...], expand: ['data.product'] })` at build time and render the pricing grid. Single source of truth = Stripe Dashboard.

---

## 6. Customer Portal — One-Click Self-Serve

Code already shown in §2. **Setup steps (one-time, ~5 min):**

1. Stripe Dashboard → Settings → Billing → **Customer portal**
2. Enable: cancel subscriptions, switch plans, update payment method, view invoices
3. Under "Products" — add Solo + Team, list both monthly + annual prices as switchable
4. Set default return URL to `https://brocco.ai/account`
5. Save → copy nothing; the portal session API now works

That's it. The "Manage Billing" button on `/account` posts to `/api/portal` and 302s to `portal.url`. Cancel, downgrade, swap card — all handled by Stripe.

---

## 7. Scary Failure Mode — Payment Fails, Customer Locked Forever

**Default Stripe behavior:** invoice.payment_failed → Smart Retries (default 4 attempts over ~3 weeks) → if all fail, subscription transitions to **`unpaid`** or **`canceled`** depending on your config (Dashboard → Billing → Subscriptions → "If all retries for a payment fail").

**The trap:** developers gate access on `status === 'active'` only. When card expires, status becomes `past_due` for ~3 weeks while Stripe retries — you've already locked them out, they don't know why, they churn instead of updating their card.

**Correct pattern:**
```ts
const ACCESS_OK = ['active', 'trialing', 'past_due'];      // give past_due users grace
const READONLY  = ['unpaid'];                              // block writes, allow read + portal
const REVOKED   = ['canceled', 'incomplete_expired'];

if (sub.status === 'past_due') {
  // Show in-app banner: "Card declined — update payment method" → link to portal
  // Continue letting them USE the product
}
```

Configure in Dashboard: **Smart Retries on (8 retries / 2 weeks), final action = "Mark as unpaid"** (NOT cancel — `unpaid` lets them recover by updating the card; `canceled` requires re-checkout). Plus enable **Card Updater** (free, automatic) so expired cards re-link without user action. Sources: `docs.stripe.com/billing/revenue-recovery/smart-retries`.

---

## 8. Env Vars + Vercel Commands

```bash
# Server-only
vercel env add STRIPE_API_KEY production               # sk_live_...
vercel env add STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET production        # whsec_... (from dashboard webhook endpoint)
vercel env add STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_MONTHLY production    # price_...
vercel env add STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_ANNUAL production     # price_...
vercel env add STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM_MONTHLY production    # price_...
vercel env add STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM_ANNUAL production     # price_...
vercel env add APP_URL production                      # https://brocco.ai

# Client-safe (only if you ever embed Elements; not needed for hosted Checkout)
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY production  # pk_live_...

# Repeat each for `preview` and `development` (use test-mode keys: sk_test_, whsec_test_, price_test_)
vercel env pull .env.local                             # sync to local

# Webhook endpoint to register in Stripe Dashboard:
#   https://brocco.ai/api/webhooks/stripe
#   Events: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.*, invoice.paid, invoice.payment_failed
```

For local webhook testing: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhooks/stripe` — outputs a `whsec_...` to put in `.env.local`.

---

## Time-to-paid estimate

After env vars: **paste-and-go in ~45 minutes.** Dashboard config (portal + webhooks + tax) is the slowest step at ~15 min.

